WEBVTT

NOTE How to download and save your goodies on a phone. Captions follow the narration.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.448
Hi there!

2
00:00:01.548 --> 00:00:09.206
In this video, I'll show you how to download your goodies on your phone, save them somewhere easy to find, and find them again later.

3
00:00:10.756 --> 00:00:12.262
First, let's sign in.

4
00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:14.705
Tap the menu button at the top left.

5
00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:17.634
Then tap Sign in.

6
00:00:21.756 --> 00:00:25.564
Enter the email and password for your account, then tap Sign in.

7
00:00:27.256 --> 00:00:28.728
Your account opens.

8
00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.283
Tap My downloads.

9
00:00:32.756 --> 00:00:36.718
Each purchase has its own card, with the order number and the version.

10
00:00:36.818 --> 00:00:39.808
When it's ready, it says one download available.

11
00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:44.019
Before you download, here's the important part.

12
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:48.554
Each digital purchase includes one download of the latest version.

13
00:00:48.654 --> 00:00:52.582
Starting the download uses it. Just looking at this page doesn't.

14
00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:56.313
And when a new version comes out, you'll get one new download of it.

15
00:00:57.663 --> 00:01:00.634
When you're ready to save it, tap Download on the card.

16
00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.717
A reminder pops up.

17
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:06.846
Read it, then tap Download now.

18
00:01:08.663 --> 00:01:11.767
A message lets you know your download has started.

19
00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:15.020
From here, your browser saves the file on your phone.

20
00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.289
Where it goes depends on your phone.

21
00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:24.116
On an iPhone or iPad, Safari saves it to the Files app, in the Downloads folder.

22
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:28.986
On Android, Chrome saves it to your Downloads, which you'll find in the Files app.

23
00:01:29.086 --> 00:01:33.951
Tip: keep all your inserts together in one folder, like one named Nurse Love.

24
00:01:35.301 --> 00:01:44.558
To find it again on an iPhone or iPad, open the Files app, tap Browse, then Downloads. If you don't see it there, check iCloud Drive.

25
00:01:44.658 --> 00:01:50.963
On Android, open the Files app and look in Downloads. Or in Chrome, tap More, then Downloads.

26
00:01:52.313 --> 00:01:56.794
Back on the website, My downloads now says Download used, with the date.

27
00:01:56.894 --> 00:02:01.013
The website can't see your phone, so it can't tell whether the file saved.

28
00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:04.208
So open the file once, just to make sure it's there.

29
00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:10.408
If the file didn't save, or it won't open, tap Report a download problem.

30
00:02:10.508 --> 00:02:13.729
A real person at the store reads every report.

31
00:02:15.079 --> 00:02:18.869
For anything else, tap Support in your account and send a message.

32
00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:20.658
You'll hear back by email.

33
00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.036
And that's it!

34
00:02:23.136 --> 00:02:27.390
Download once, save it somewhere easy to find, and open it to check.

35
00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.905
Thanks for watching.
